The model gateway image (deploy/litellm)

OspreyFlow's own gateway image is built from the MIT-licensed files of the litellm project, as
PyPI publishes them: litellm 1.101.0 and litellm-proxy-extras 0.4.94. It is not derived from the
publisher's image, and it carries neither the publisher's commercially licensed folder (the
"enterprise" directory its top-level licence carves out) nor its proprietary package: the one
override file keeps the package out of the install, and the build's licence gate
(licence_gate.py) fails the build if either is found.

docker/prod_entrypoint.sh and docker/entrypoint.sh are copied unchanged from the project's
repository at revision 18243cd7 (the revision the pinned image was built from), where they are
MIT-licensed like the rest of the repository outside that directory. Their SHA-256 digests are
held by the test that guards this folder:
  prod_entrypoint.sh  6265520d64e737623031e0d421dbd58675c5e20bba06cfe4172706b9d5fd9558
  entrypoint.sh       28d6fd672a96d22be895c0d7f457aeb4beb28c11d3c0d3e799cbbef4c47869c7

